<p>New devalued green rates came into force today for Belgium, Denmark,  Holland, Germany, Spain, Portugal and Austria. Today is also the start  of the fourth confirmation period for the UK RMG. On the basis of  exchange rates today, the UK RMG is greater than +5 per cent, at 9.256  peer cent.  It is, therefore currently forecast to enter its fifth  and final confirmation period on 11 August prior to a possible revaluation  on 21 August. All currencies with negative RMGs for this period will  devalue on 11 August tomorrow by reducing their gaps  to zero. Hence,  further green rate devaluations are currently forecast for Denmark,  Spain and Portugal. The next confirmation period will run from 11-20  August. During confirmation periods the 3-day (6 per cent) rule is</p>
